1
00:03:42,000 --> 00:03:48,000
The adventure of a lifetime begins with one small pebble.

2
00:07:24,000 --> 00:07:30,000
The Pebble and the Penguin is a animation, adventure,
family film directed by Don Bluth.

3
00:11:06,000 --> 00:11:12,000
A bashful bachelor penguin named Hubie, who's
partial to a pretty female named Marina.

4
00:14:48,000 --> 00:14:54,000
Ancient penguin ritual dictates that males present a
pebble to their intended, then mate for life.

5
00:18:30,000 --> 00:18:36,000
Hubie finds a spiffy stone, but before he can bestow it on Marina, dastardly rival
Drake tosses him into the churning sea, and Hubie gets swept away.

6
00:22:12,000 --> 00:22:18,000
Hubie (voice), played by Martin Short.

7
00:25:54,000 --> 00:26:00,000
Marina (voice), played by Annie Golden.

8
00:29:36,000 --> 00:29:42,000
Rocko (voice), played by Jim Belushi.

9
00:33:18,000 --> 00:33:24,000
Drake (voice), played by Tim Curry.

10
00:37:00,000 --> 00:37:06,000
Petra (voice), played by Alissa King.

11
00:40:42,000 --> 00:40:48,000
Priscilla / Chinstrap (voice), played by Stevie Vallance.

12
00:44:24,000 --> 00:44:30,000
The Pebble and the Penguin is a 1995 American independent animated musical
romance comedy-adventure film directed by Don Bluth and Gary Goldman.

13
00:48:06,000 --> 00:48:12,000
The film stars the voices of Martin Short, Jim
Belushi, Tim Curry, and Annie Golden.

14
00:51:48,000 --> 00:51:54,000
Based on the true life mating rituals of the Adélie penguins in Antarctica, the film focuses on a timid, stuttering penguin named Hubie who tries to impress a beautiful penguin named Marina by giving her a pebble that
fell from the sky and keep her from the clutches of an evil penguin named Drake who wants Marina for himself, causing Hubie to team up with a cantankerous yet good-hearted rockhopper penguin named Rocko.

15
00:55:30,000 --> 00:55:36,000
Towards the end of production, Metro-Goldwyn-Mayer Pictures significantly changed the film, resulting
in Bluth and Goldman leaving the film and asking to have their names taken off of it.

16
00:59:12,000 --> 00:59:18,000
The two would later start working at Fox Animation Studios.

17
01:02:54,000 --> 01:03:00,000
The film was released in the United States on April 12, 1995, by MGM/UA Distribution Co., was panned by
critics and became a box office failure, grossing $3.9 million against a $28 million budget.

18
01:06:36,000 --> 01:06:42,000
It is the final film to be produced by Don Bluth Limited before
the studio went bankrupt and ceased operations.

19
01:10:18,000 --> 01:10:24,000
The tone is lighthearted and emotional.
